WEBVTT

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:10.490
Hamamatsu, home of yummy eel...

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:19.270
Fujinomiya, land of tasty shigure...

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.620
I must have come pretty far up.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.040
What a nice view.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:42.880
<i>I might spoil the view from the 
campsite if I enjoy it now!</i>

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:46.000
I see nothing.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:52.980
Do I go straight from here?

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.370
This area's looking more forested.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.900
It must be scary walking here at night.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.430
Hello!

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:03.950
Hello.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:07.040
<b>Fujikawa Healthy
Greenspace Campsite</b>

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.320
<i>I made it to the campsite!</i>

00:02:55.610 --> 00:03:02.530
<b>(2) Episode 8 
Camping Alone</b>

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:00.280
It's so open!

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:17.060
I can still see Mt. Fuji, too!

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.190
The washroom's so clean.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.710
This is the cooking pavilion.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:26.640
I'm not allowed to make a 
fire outside of here, right?

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:31.390
I can't have a campfire, but it's not 
too cold, so I guess it's all right.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.240
I could camp in the rain!

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.350
I can't connect to the internet...

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.110
Hello!

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:44.060
Hello.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:45.320
Hello!

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.870
It's a relief to know there 
are other campers around.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:25.780
<i>This view must be really nice at night.</i>

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:30.680
<i>You can see all the way to Izu.</i>

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:37.480
Well...

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:41.210
Time to start solo camping!

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:47.330
Home of yummy eel...

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:58.400
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.550
Oh, I think I can fix it.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:18.140
Tent's all set!

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:22.830
It's a lot of work doing it alone.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.750
Now...

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:28.700
Rin-chan said solo camping is boring 
if you don't have anything to do.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.000
For me, it's gotta be...

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:31.930
this!

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:35.180
Shimeji

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:35.180
Salmon Fillets

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:35.180
<b>Tokaido Butter</b>

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:34.040
Outdoor cooking research!

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:39.940
Aluminum Foil

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:39.940
<i>If it's good, I can share it with the 
others when we go camping together.</i>

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:43.990
<i>As long as I'm cooking for myself,
 it's no bother to anyone if I mess up.</i>

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:49.570
What are you doing, Onee-chan?

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:53.000
That girl's camping on her own.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.590
Maybe she's a loner.

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:55.580
A loner?

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:57.500
<i>No...</i>

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.830
Max Height 3.4 m\h\h\hMax Width 3.5 m

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.830
Closed for winter

00:05:58.490 --> 00:05:59.950
<i>Not again...</i>

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:04.410
<i>Just kidding.</i>

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.340
<i>I read about this yesterday.</i>

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:12.360
<i>This tunnel leads to Yashajin Pass, doesn't it?</i>

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:16.680
<i>So creepy.</i>

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:21.920
<i>I would've been really 
let down if I hadn't known,</i>

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:25.250
<i>but there's something awe-inspiring 
about seeing it like this.</i>

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.150
<i>I guess it's that wabi-sabi aesthetic.</i>

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:10.030
Hayakawa

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:18.490
<i>I still love quiet lakes.</i>

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:24.170
<i>I think the campsite is around there,</i>

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:28.240
<i>and that road leads to Shizuoka.</i>

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:34.300
Rindou Ikawa Amehata Line

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:31.550
<i>The Rindou Ikawa Amehata Line
 is the only route</i>

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:38.410
<i>that takes you from Yamanashi 
to Lake Ikawa in Shizuoka.</i>

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:44.900
<i>The road's under repair 
right now after falling apart.</i>

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.440
Caution

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.400
<i>I want to try taking it once it's open again.</i>

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:53.630
<i>A suspension bridge...</i>

00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:00.260
<i>It's sturdier than I thought.</i>

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.030
The middle part rocks!

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:12.120
<i>Wait, the trail past the 
bridge looks even worse...</i>

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:16.710
<i>I should go back and hit the hot spring.</i>

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:23.410
<i>Deer.</i>

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:24.230
<i>Bear.</i>

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.800
<i>Boar.</i>

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:29.770
<i>I've heard deer isn't too gamey...</i>

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:37.940
<i>Actually, isn't the braised bear paw in 
high-end Chinese restaurants game, too?</i>

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.250
Search

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:42.250
braised bear paw recipe

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:41.920
<i>Is it even something you can prepare at home?</i>

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:55.260
Braised
Bear
Paw

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:44.370
<i>Braised bear paw.</i>

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:48.960
<i>First, stew the bear paw with ginger 
and green onion for four or five hours</i>

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.430
<i>to get rid of the smell.</i>

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:55.260
<i>After that, use tweezers to remove all hairs.</i>

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:59.600
<i>Once that's done, stew it for 
another four hours or so until tender.</i>

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.490
<i>Remove the outer skin, bone, and claws.</i>

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:04.270
<i>That completes the preparations. 
We're now ready to start cooking.</i>

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:05.720
Hello.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:07.270
I'd like some of this deer meat.

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:10.800
Welcome!

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:11.020
Welcome

00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:16.580
<i>Hot springs are the best when 
they're on the particularly hot side.</i>

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:21.610
<i>There's a cafeteria here.</i>

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:24.200
<i>Maybe I'll go to the campsite 
after I'm done eating.</i>

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.980
<i>I should send a photo of Lake Amehata.</i>

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:33.470
<i>Come to think of it, 
Nadeshiko's stopped sending me photos.</i>

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.770
<i>She hasn't read my messages, either.</i>

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:38.780
<i>I wonder why...</i>

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:42.680
<b>Nadeshiko</b>

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:42.680
<b>Calling</b>

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:44.230
<i>The customer you have dialed 
has switched off their phone</i>

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:47.190
<i>or is out of the service area.</i>

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:49.640
<i>It's up in the mountains over there.</i>

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:51.420
<i>She must be out of range.</i>

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:53.240
<i>Probably.</i>

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:06.830
<i>Nadeshiko is just out of range.</i>

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:11.240
<i>Nadeshiko is just out of range.</i>

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:15.920
<i>Nadeshiko is just out of range...</i>

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:18.720
<i>Is she really?</i>

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:33.140
<i>Darn it!</i>

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:34.820
<i>It's going to bug me.</i>

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:39.240
<i>I'm the reason she decided 
to go camping on her own.</i>

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:43.680
<i>I'm sure I'm just being a worrywart, but...</i>

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.000
I'm gonna go shopping and then head to the campsite!

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:59.010
Fujikawa Healthy Greenspace Campsite

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:15.040
Should we have dinner?

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:16.020
Okay.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:21.800
Are you sure you two are happy with 
convenience store meals for a camping trip?

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:22.430
Yeah.

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:24.780
We all like different things, anyway.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:26.920
It's a lot of work for you to cook, isn't it?

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:30.290
I wouldn't have minded cooking for once.

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:34.460
This is better than the food he does cook.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.570
I know.

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:37.800
I heard that.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:40.430
Okay, we'll go warm up yours, too.

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:41.200
Okay.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:42.430
Be careful.

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:03.930
Onee-chan, what is that girl doing?

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:06.300
An unholy ritual?

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:11.220
<i>Tonight's dinner is whole 
veggies roasted in foil.</i>

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:31.600
Outdoor Cooking
Experiments

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:31.600
Whole veggies
roasted in foil

00:12:12.050 --> 00:12:14.680
<i>First, give the veggies a quick rinse.</i>

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:18.250
<i>Root veggies should be wrapped in 
wet newspaper and aluminum foil.</i>

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:23.230
<i>Other veggies should be wrapped 
in foil and tossed into the fire.</i>

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:21.940
<i>Hot!</i>

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:21.940
Hot

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:24.990
<i>Then you wait.</i>

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:31.440
<i>Use smaller, thinner root vegetables 
to ensure that they cook evenly.</i>

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:35.100
Sweet Potato: 30 mins

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:35.100
<i>Different veggies require 
different cooking times.</i>

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:35.100
Carrot: 30 mins

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:35.100
Tomato: 10 mins

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:35.100
Eggplant: 10 mins

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.100
Potato: 30 mins

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.100
Gummies: 5 secs

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:35.100
Avocado: 10 mins

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:35.100
Garlic: 5 mins

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.110
<b>Beep Beep Beep</b>

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:37.860
<i>Shazam!</i>

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:43.860
<i>Retrieve the items before they burn,
then season them lightly...</i>

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.610
Herb salt

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:43.860
Olive oil

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:46.620
Roasted Tomato

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.080
<i>And you're done.</i>

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:50.410
She's cooking in foil!

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.410
Yum!

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.340
There's nowhere else we can use a stove...

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:57.860
I feel awkward about going in.

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:07.400
What should we do?

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:09.220
Huh?!

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:13.780
Onee-chan, roasted tomato is super good!

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:15.700
When did you get over there?!

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:18.370
What's this?

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:19.650
Potato.

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:20.920
And this one?

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:21.960
Um...

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:23.400
I think that was a carrot.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.780
Hey, have some restraint.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:27.350
Why, though?

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:28.660
It's all right.

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:31.050
Would you like some, miss?

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:32.950
I have baked apples, too.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:36.160
<i>She's a witch.</i>

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:40.100
So you're camping with your dad, huh?

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:40.860
Yeah.

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:43.620
Mom's out traveling with her friends.

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:45.840
She said it's a housewives' retreat.

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:47.680
Are you having fun camping?

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:50.280
I dunno.

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:53.180
All we've done is eat snacks and watch anime.

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:54.910
I see.

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.190
The next one's done!

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:00.900
What's that?

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:02.680
Whole roasted eggplant.

00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:04.190
Help yourselves.

00:14:05.980 --> 00:14:07.100
Yum!

00:14:07.100 --> 00:14:09.190
You should have some, too.

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:11.210
Okay...

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:17.970
I never knew eggplant got so runny.

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:22.480
Next up, potato!

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:25.150
The skin's so crunchy. 
It's like a potato chip!

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:27.970
I like the skin more than the inside.

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:31.470
Next, whole roasted avocado!

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:37.290
This one might be better raw...

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:41.490
Wait, weren't you making 
something over there?

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:48.020
I think it could use a little more time.

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:51.990
I never knew you could warm 
up packed meals this way.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:55.390
Outdoor cooking seemed hard.

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:57.630
It might not be authentic, but...

00:14:58.250 --> 00:14:59.500
That's not true.

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:03.390
I love having instant noodles when I camp.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:10.130
Now, I'll let you have some of my favorite...

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:13.640
Fire-roasted sweet potato!

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.280
I think they turned out good.

00:15:18.590 --> 00:15:20.220
It's so sweet!

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:25.140
All I did was wrap it in foil 
and put it in the fire.

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:27.960
Did you use high-quality potatoes for this?

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:29.030
No.

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:33.530
<b>Sweet Potatoes

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:33.530
<b>Sweet Potatoes</b>

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:33.530
<b>Sweet Potatoes</b>

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:33.530
<b>Sweet Potatoes</b>

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:33.530
<b>Sweet Potatoes</b>

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:31.710
They were on sale at the supermarket.

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:33.110
Huh...

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:36.620
<i>I never knew it was so easy.</i>

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:40.730
You could get started
 just grilling meat, really.

00:15:40.730 --> 00:15:43.540
Camp cooking is fun.

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:47.860
And even if you mess up and end up 
with something weird, it's still fun.

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.620
The carrot turned black!

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:53.790
Y-You're right! I overcooked it!

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:55.590
It's so bitter!

00:15:55.590 --> 00:15:57.000
It's charred to ash!

00:15:58.330 --> 00:15:59.930
Yuck!

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:01.520
This might be okay...

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:03.140
I can't eat this! It's too bitter!

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:04.940
This is how grown-ups like it!

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:06.940
Haruka? Hiroto?

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:07.930
Dad!

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:10.680
You've been gone for a while. I got worried.

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:12.910
Oh... sorry.

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:15.200
You'll have to excuse my kids.

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:16.630
Oh, not at all.

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:18.380
I was the one who invited them.

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:21.250
Hey, try this.

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:29.550
It's a bit bitter...

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:36.290
Well, thank you for the food.

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:38.210
You're very welcome.

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:39.960
Bye, Onee-chan!

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:41.170
Bye.

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:42.780
Bye!

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:43.480
<b>No signal</b>

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:46.790
<i>So she really was just out of range.</i>

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:50.400
<i>And she's already made friends.</i>

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:54.240
<i>Nadeshiko's amazing.</i>

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:59.990
Dad, I think I'll cook something
 the next time we come.

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:02.270
Even if it's something simple.

00:17:03.650 --> 00:17:04.780
Sounds good.

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:08.650
Why don't we come with Mom next time?

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:09.520
Yeah!

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:14.820
<i>I should have just camped at Amehata.</i>

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:17.530
<i>I'll have dinner on the way back...</i>

00:17:29.970 --> 00:17:32.860
Dad, are there deer or anything around here?

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:34.530
I'm not sure...

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:39.380
S-Sakura-san! You're here, too?

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:42.540
I'm sorry. Did I scare you?

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:46.500
Were you worried about Nadeshiko?

00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:50.580
Well, I guess...

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:54.480
It was partly my fault for 
suggesting things, so...

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:58.280
Thanks, Rin-chan.

00:18:00.210 --> 00:18:03.030
What are you going to do now, Sakura-san?

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:04.210
I'm going home.

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:06.310
She seems all right on her own.

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:08.350
What about you?

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:09.890
I'm leaving, too.

00:18:10.570 --> 00:18:13.140
This is Nadeshiko's solo camping trip.

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:18.010
Um...

00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:20.820
Since we're here, why don't we visit the top?

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.790
I heard this place is 
famous for its nightscape.

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:25.570
Sounds good.

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:33.820
Wow... This is a pretty amazing night view.

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:34.740
It is.

00:18:34.740 --> 00:18:41.110
Lake Motosu, home of yummy curry noodles...

00:18:39.020 --> 00:18:40.710
Ack! Nadeshiko!

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:53.220
It really is pretty!

00:18:55.430 --> 00:18:56.640
All right.

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:07.340
What do you think she's doing?

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:09.600
Maybe her phone broke.

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:19.630
<b>No signal</b>

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:30.890
Nadeshiko

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:41.910
Is something wrong?

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:51.920
I'm out of range, but solo camping is fun!

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:58.140
Rin-chan, why don't we go into town?

00:19:58.720 --> 00:20:00.200
I'll buy you dinner.

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:02.320
Okay.

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:35.580
I dream on...

00:22:37.050 --> 00:22:39.540
<b>Inu Inu Inuko-san</b>

00:22:37.840 --> 00:22:39.540
Inu Inu Inuko-san!

00:22:40.610 --> 00:22:43.750
Caribou-kun is so cute.

00:22:43.890 --> 00:22:46.890
You sure do like Caribou-kun, Aoi-chan.

00:22:46.890 --> 00:22:50.010
I wish we had one at the Minobu branch.

00:22:50.240 --> 00:22:53.510
I heard they sell plushies 
at the Minobu Caribou.

00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:54.760
No way.

00:22:54.760 --> 00:22:58.020
It's got to be life-sized so you can hug it.

00:22:58.220 --> 00:23:01.920
I heard you can buy the giant Caribou-kun.

00:23:01.920 --> 00:23:03.520
What?! Really?!

00:23:04.600 --> 00:23:07.420
<i>We're at the campsite, Caribou-kun.</i>

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:08.780
<i>Indeed.</i>

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:09.510
Indeed

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:12.500
<i>The campfire's so pretty,
isn't it, Caribou-kun?</i>

00:23:12.430 --> 00:23:14.470
Indeed

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:13.530
<i>Indeed.</i>

00:23:14.540 --> 00:23:16.950
<i>Goodnight, Caribou-kun.</i>

00:23:16.810 --> 00:23:18.560
Indeed

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:18.400
<i>Indeed.</i>

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:25.040
Caribou-kun

00:23:22.990 --> 00:23:24.250
What did I expect?

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:35.260
Next Episode

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:35.260
<b>Winter's End and the Day of Departure</b>

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:41.260
When camping...

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:41.260
Always mind the campsite 
and facility rules. Don't forget to 
take care of fires and your trash!

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:41.260
It gets cold during the winter. 
Stay warm and be well-prepared!

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:41.260
Outdoor Activities Club
